    <heading level="1">Section 7.3 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Recognize a Preliminary Strategy to Factor Polynomials Completely</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, identify the best method to use to factor each polynomial.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="135" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ $$10q^{2} + 50$$</item>
          <item>ⓑ $$a^{2} - 5a - 14$$</item>
          <item>ⓒ $$uv + 2u + 3v + 6$$</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ factor the GCF, binomial ⓑ Undo FOIL ⓒ factor by grouping</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="136" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
